From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 86b34e01 <86b34e01@invalid>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 14:43:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Drop duplicate AddShortCache entries instead of throwing

When InvalidateRangeImpl walks a modified pool chunk, it calls
AddShortCache once per stale slot whose texture has HasOneReference().
Two slots can have byte-equal cached descriptors that point at distinct
Texture instances with different Info: DescriptorCache[id] is updated
on every slot re-population, but a re-population that hits the texture
cache returns an existing Texture whose Info reflects its earlier
creation descriptor rather than the current one. The two slots' cached
descriptors converge while the textures' Info diverges; the second
AddShortCache call then throws ArgumentException on the duplicate
descriptor key.

Convert the lookup add to TryAdd and return early on duplicates. This
prevents the crash but is a crash-vs-wrong-render trade rather than a
structurally safe no-op: the kept entry's Texture.Info may disagree
with its key descriptor, so a later FindShortCache hit could surface a
texture with the wrong format / width / range. The InvalidatedSequence
check in FindShortCache bounds staleness but does not catch the Info
mismatch.

TODO: replace dedup with a deeper fix once FindOrCreateTexture's role
in producing distinct Textures for byte-equal descriptors is understood
(likely guest gpuVa remapping between slot populations).
---
 .../Image/AutoDeleteCache.cs                  | 30 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Gpu/Image/AutoDeleteCache.cs b/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Gpu/Image/AutoDeleteCache.cs
index 99b34112f..0c2fa68ad 100644
--- a/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Gpu/Image/AutoDeleteCache.cs
+++ b/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Gpu/Image/AutoDeleteCache.cs
@@ -278,8 +278,36 @@ namespace Ryujinx.Graphics.Gpu.Image
         {
             ShortTextureCacheEntry entry = new(descriptor, texture);
 
+            // The lookup is descriptor-keyed. Two pool slots can have byte-equal cached
+            // descriptors yet hold distinct Texture instances with different Info
+            // (different format, width, physical range). DescriptorCache[id] is updated
+            // on every slot re-population, but a re-population that hits the texture
+            // cache returns an existing Texture whose Info reflects its earlier creation
+            // descriptor rather than the current one -- the two slots' cached descriptors
+            // converge while the textures' Info diverges. Both Texture instances then
+            // have HasOneReference()==true and pass the gate in InvalidateRangeImpl.
+            //
+            // Dedup here converts the otherwise-fatal duplicate-key on the second
+            // Dictionary.Add into a soft failure: the kept entry's Texture.Info may
+            // disagree with its key descriptor, so a later FindShortCache hit could
+            // surface a texture with the wrong format / width / range. This is a
+            // crash-vs-wrong-render trade, NOT a structurally safe no-op. The
+            // InvalidatedSequence check in FindShortCache bounds staleness but does
+            // not catch the Info mismatch.
+            //
+            // The same-Texture-shared-across-slots case the original commit attributed
+            // the duplicate to cannot reach here -- a shared instance has refcount >= 2
+            // and HasOneReference() filters it out before AddShortCache is called.
+            //
+            // TODO(86b34e01): replace dedup with a deeper fix once FindOrCreateTexture's
+            // role in producing distinct Textures for byte-equal descriptors is
+            // understood (likely guest gpuVa remapping between slot populations).
+            if (!_shortCacheLookup.TryAdd(entry.Descriptor, entry))
+            {
+                return;
+            }
+
             _shortCacheBuilder.Add(entry);
-            _shortCacheLookup.Add(entry.Descriptor, entry);
 
             texture.ShortCacheEntry = entry;
 
